Author: Steve Liao (TVC) <steveliao@google.com>
Date:   Mon Mar 30 08:24:27 2026 +0000

    ANDROID: ioctl: Use kernel_page_size for VMA page size validation
    
    The ioctl10 test compares the vma_page_size returned by the kernel against
    the userspace page size. On x86_64 systems running 16K page size
    emulation, getpagesize() returns the emulated userspace size, which may
    not match the underlying kernel page size expected in the VMA.
    
    Switch to kernel_page_size() from pgsize_helpers.h to ensure the test
    validates against the actual kernel configuration, preventing failures
    under emulation.
    
    Test: atest vts_ltp_test_x86_64:syscalls.ioctl10_64bit#syscalls.ioctl10_64bit -- --abi x86_64
    Bug: 486903917
    Bug: 481846501
    Change-Id: Ie487f6640b82df8d8e316ab80b2fe39875b838e8
    Signed-off-by: Steve Liao <steveliao@google.com>

diff --git a/testcases/kernel/syscalls/ioctl/ioctl10.c b/testcases/kernel/syscalls/ioctl/ioctl10.c
index b668c9e93..c3120c2e3 100644
--- a/testcases/kernel/syscalls/ioctl/ioctl10.c
+++ b/testcases/kernel/syscalls/ioctl/ioctl10.c
@@ -25,6 +25,7 @@
 #include <sys/sysmacros.h>
 #include <linux/fs.h>
 #include "lapi/ioctl.h"
+#include "pgsize_helpers.h"
 
 #define PROC_MAP_PATH "/proc/self/maps"
 
@@ -106,7 +107,7 @@ static void verify_ioctl(void)
 	TST_EXP_EQ_LU(q->vma_flags, entry.vm_flags);
 	TST_EXP_EQ_LU(q->vma_start, entry.vm_start);
 	TST_EXP_EQ_LU(q->vma_end, entry.vm_end);
-	TST_EXP_EQ_LU(q->vma_page_size, getpagesize());
+	TST_EXP_EQ_LU(q->vma_page_size, kernel_page_size());
 	TST_EXP_EQ_LU(q->vma_offset, entry.vm_pgoff);
 	TST_EXP_EQ_LU(q->inode, entry.vm_inode);
 	TST_EXP_EQ_LU(q->dev_major, entry.vm_major);
